<title>FRANCE: Six ships loading wheat in Rouen, three more due.</title>
<headline>Six ships loading wheat in Rouen, three more due.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six ships were loading 74,000 tonnes of wheat in Rouen, port officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The wheat was for export to west Africa, Iraq and Italy, they said.</p>
<p>Three more ships were expected in port very shortly to load 33,000 tonnes of wheat. The destination was not specified.</p>
<p>One more vessel was also due in port to load 60,000 tonnes of barley.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
